From a1525ff508affa711607dfb166215a3bbdc1fe7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xukongyang <xukongyang@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:05:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] derphttp, magicsock: push rotated admission credentials
 to live clients

SetDERPAuth only updated the credentials stored for regions not yet
dialed: each derphttp.Client snapshotted the token at creation, so
after a derper restart long-lived clients reconnected forever with
the stale token and the admission controller kept rejecting them
until the process itself restarted.

Give derphttp.Client a SetAuth method guarding the fields with a
leaf mutex, read them under that lock when a connection is
established, and have magicsock's SetDERPAuth push the new
credentials into the already-active clients too. The next
reconnection then presents the current token; rotation timers keep
long-lived connections admissible across derper restarts.

Tested with a reconnect regression test (a fake admission
controller records which token each connection presented; before
this change the reconnection after BreakConnection kept sending
the old token) and -race across the derphttp package.
